--- body ---
## Context
Unticketed prerequisite of 0026's golden gate (review-implementation.md §3,
a panel document now lost; DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-31): no pinned fixture corpus
exists — bench/queries.txt is 16 queries, and every
answer-set artifact was measured against the author's private library, which
cannot be committed. Needed: a committable multilingual document set, ~40
queries, pinned answer sets at k=10, and a harness that builds an index over
it WITHOUT Zotero. The thresholds the gate then enforces live once in
SPEC.md §5.2.8.

Rulings of 2026-09-02 (DECISIONS.md, "The golden fixture corpus") reshape the
work. What the corpus is: a source recipe (archive identifier, byte hash, item
metadata, licence basis per document), an injection script into a collection
of a public Zotero library, and a committed export of the items JSON and each
attachment's `/fulltext` JSON, replayed by the harness through 0026's mock
local API. The committed `text.txt` files of PR #151 are superseded by that
export: zoteus indexes Zotero's client extraction, and the probe measured
word-set Jaccard 0,39–0,61 between it and `pdftotext`, with a 100-page cap and
no page breaks. Where a document may come from: a public archive identifier,
never a personal library; versioned open archives (arXiv vN, Zenodo version
DOI, HAL id with version) beside Gallica, Internet Archive, Wikimedia Commons
and Wikisource revision ids; no self-deposit. Zotero #6012's calibration
corpus stays out.

## Re-sourcing PR #151's 19 documents (ruling 2)
| status | documents | action |
|---|---|---|
| compliant | Johnson, Baudelaire, Stein, Curie, Einstein-Minkowski (archive.org) | keep; record identifier + hash |
| archive named, fetched by key | Cournot (Gallica), Walras, Porte, Minkowski (Internet Archive), Decision 11/2017 (FAOLEX `LEX-FAOC179224`, admitted 2026-09-02: docs/pdf URL, hash, LEX id, Wayback date) | record identifier, re-fetch from the archive, compare hash |
| library-only or non-archive host | Malynes, Ramsey (full first editions on archive.org), Depitre (Gallica), Neurath (dropped: no admitted archive holds it); Circulars 25/2016, 41/2010, 42/2010 (dropped: Wikisource holds no circular as text; the 1992 constitution, vi + en, is the administrative register); Habilitation (HAL, versioned); Highway Code (UK Government Web Archive snapshot, or drop) | re-source or drop |

## Vietnamese slice, rebuilt (ruling 5)
- Administrative register: the 1992 constitution on vi.wikisource, pinned by
  `oldid`; Wikisource holds no ministerial circular as text (checked 2026-09-02).
- Scientific register: three HAL records in Vietnamese (OUV, ART, COMM), versioned;
  HAL serves a challenge page to scripts, so their bytes are pinned by hand.
- Cross-lingual anchors for R29: des Michels' Lục Vân Tiên and Kim Vân Kiều
  (Gallica, FR–VN in one scan); a constitution in vi.wikisource and its
  English text in en.wikisource (EN–VN); Bonet 1899 (Internet Archive, VN–FR
  dictionary, pairs with Johnson); Decision 11/2017 with its official English
  translation, from FAOLEX (admitted 2026-09-02, vbpl.vn not).
- Same work in two shapes: Việt Nam sử lược as a Commons scan and as a
  Wikisource transcription.
- Chinese-script bonus for the SHOULD tier: Đại Việt sử ký toàn thư's original.
- Out: Internet Archive's Vietnamese Marx/Lenin translations (translators'
  rights); anything from Gallica's 1922–1954 deposit whose author is not
  life+70 clear.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] every fixture document carries a public archive identifier, a byte hash,
      and a licence basis in the source recipe; none is sourced from a personal
      library (ruling 2); versioned identifiers where the archive offers them
      (ruling 3)
- [ ] the re-sourcing table above executed: 5 recorded, 5 re-fetched, 9
      re-sourced or dropped, each outcome logged (recipe landed in PR #177;
      10 entries still await a browser fetch and hash)
- [ ] the Vietnamese MUST tier rebuilt from admitted archives per the slice
      above, with no self-deposit (rulings 4, 5)
- [ ] injection script: collection in a public library, linked-file
      attachments, client version and the two indexing preferences recorded
- [ ] export snapshot committed (items JSON + `/fulltext` JSON per attachment),
      with the re-pin procedure documented as re-export, diff as review artifact
- [ ] Zotero-free index-build harness in bench/ replaying the export through
      0026's mock local API
- [ ] a cross-lingual slice: EN and FR queries whose pinned answer sets are
      Vietnamese entries, gated separately from the monolingual queries so a
      regression names which of R7 and R29 it broke (R29 ratified 2026-08-31;
      SPEC.md §5.2.8 owns the thresholds, this ticket pins them)
- [ ] ~40 queries with pinned answer sets, each labelled by facet, language
      lane and carrying signal (exact string / paraphrase / agreement); no
      difficulty tiers
- [ ] 0026's golden gate consumes it in make check
- [ ] R33's three probe shapes present: a rare exact string, a paraphrase sharing
      no content word with its answer, and an agreement case
- [ ] R34's reading supported: every pinned answer inside the first ten, absolute,
      beside the stability reading of the same sets
- [ ] the intersections carried, not one axis at a time: a monster in a non-Latin
      script, and a scale run at the multilingual default
- [ ] a group-library slice in a closed group, per the perimeter ruling; no trash
      and no feed slice
- [ ] passage-length distribution pinned beside the export (SPEC.md §5.2.8)
- [ ] SPEC.md §5.2.8's fixture description updated to the three-layer shape
